# Force LF for all text files on checkout, on every machine.
#
# MC manifests (_mc/MANIFEST.json, .claude/framework-manifest.json) and
# the regression-seed enforcer (BC-02 drift, BC-05 staleness) RAW-HASH
# working-tree bytes. A mixed or CRLF working tree (Windows git core.autocrlf=true)
# corrupts those hashes and false-REDs the enforcer — which, as of 0.17.0, blocks
# sprint-close and release. Forcing LF for text makes the working tree match the
# LF-hashed manifest on every checkout. See RI-001.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binaries — never normalize (defense-in-depth; text=auto already detects).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
